---
title: States of the relying party (Satoshi) and the resolver
---

%% One state machine for the channel peer that verifies Stuart's keys.
%% The Resolving state follows the Resolve operation of the specification.

stateDiagram-v2
    state "No verified key for Stuart" as Unknown
    state "Trusted: Stuart's keys at version N" as Trusted
    state "Resolving Stuart's DID" as Resolving {
        state "Decode the DID" as Decode
        state "Process Sidecar Data:<br/>lookup tables, Genesis Document (x1)" as Sidecar
        state "Establish current_document (version 1)" as Establish
        state "Find Beacon Signals of new Beacon Addresses<br/>(minConf or more confirmations)" as Find
        state "Process Next Update" as Next
        state outcome <<choice>>
        state "didDocument resolved" as Resolved

        [*] --> Decode
        Decode --> Sidecar
        Sidecar --> Establish
        Establish --> Find
        Find --> Next
        Next --> outcome
        outcome --> Find: update applied, duplicate confirmed,<br/>or tuple of a removed Beacon Address ignored
        outcome --> Resolved: no more updates, deactivated,<br/>or versionId or versionTime reached
        Resolved --> [*]
    }
    state check <<choice>>
    state "Missing data: ask Stuart for complete Sidecar Data" as AskData
    state "Rejected: keep the last trusted version" as Rejected
    state "Channel closed: DID deactivated" as Closed

    [*] --> Unknown
    Unknown --> Resolving: first contact (did and Sidecar Data)
    Trusted --> Trusted: message signed with a trusted key (accept)
    Trusted --> Resolving: message signed with an unknown key,<br/>new Sidecar Data, or periodic check
    Resolving --> check: didDocument and didDocumentMetadata
    Resolving --> AskData: MISSING_UPDATE_DATA, or NOT_FOUND
    Resolving --> Rejected: INVALID_DID, INVALID_SIGNAL_DATA,<br/>INVALID_DID_UPDATE, or LATE_PUBLISHING
    AskData --> Resolving: more Sidecar Data received
    check --> Closed: deactivated = true
    check --> Trusted: versionId ≥ N and the message key<br/>is in authentication (accept, N = versionId)
    check --> Rejected: the message key is not authorized
    Rejected --> Trusted: continue with the last trusted keys
    Rejected --> Unknown: no trusted keys yet (first contact)
    Closed --> [*]
